Pass desktop notifications (OSC 9 and OSC 777;notify) through to the client.

mosh-server parses everything into a framebuffer, and an OSC it does not model
is discarded, so a notification from a remote program never reaches the local
terminal. This carries the latest one in the framebuffer and has the client
re-emit it, the same way the bell and the OSC 52 clipboard already travel.

A notification is an event, not state, so it is counted like `bell_count`
rather than compared by content: the same text twice still arrives twice. RIS
leaves the count alone, as it does the bell's. Notifications posted between two
state syncs collapse to the newest one.

Based on upstream PR #1144 (open and conflicting since 2021), without its OSC
1337 file transfer and with the counter in place of its content comparison,
which swallowed identical repeats:

  https://github.com/mobile-shell/mosh/pull/1144

Both ends need it. A patched server talking to a stock client is harmless: the
client's parser drops the unknown OSC.

